From 9e4d9ef65eb4eab49bfd8c389b18a27d61f3ebaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenATV <oe-alliance@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] stb: restore stable Mali GLES mode and separate GUI size

HiSilicon's Mali EGL surface represents the physical Full-HD display and is
not a switchable Kodi window. Writing fb0 and exposing both HIFB geometries as
Kodi modes lets the display settings page persist a stale resolution index;
the GUI is then magnified or cropped while the video plane remains correct.

Restore the legacy fbdev behaviour: never change fb0 and expose one stable
physical mode. Carry the independently selectable GUI size in iWidth/iHeight,
using Kodi's existing videoscreen.limitguisize setting. Full HD is the default
and 720p remains available as a manual low-resource OSD choice.

